Most web agencies will work with anyone who has a budget. That's understandable — but it often means that small businesses end up deprioritised in favour of bigger, more profitable accounts. The tradesperson or sole trader is squeezed in around the corporate client, and the results reflect that.

NC Digital doesn't work that way. We work exclusively with small businesses — local trades, sole traders, start-ups, community organisations, and independent businesses across South Wales. That's not a limitation. It's a choice.

## Why We Made That Choice

When I started NC Digital in 2025 — after 11 years as a professional web developer, and having built my first website back in 2008 — it was specifically to serve the kind of businesses that were being underserved by the agency market. Tradespeople paying thousands for websites that were built quickly and never maintained. Small businesses getting generic templates with agency branding and no real thought behind the SEO or structure. Owners who felt like they didn't fully understand what they were getting — or getting back for their money.

The businesses that needed good websites the most were often the ones getting the worst deal.

Focusing exclusively on small businesses means we understand their context completely. The budget constraints are real, not abstract. The need to generate enquiries quickly matters. The fact that the website is often the whole of a business's marketing presence — not one channel among many — shapes how we build everything.

## What It Means in Practice

**Every client is treated like the main client.** Because no one is competing with a larger account for attention, smaller businesses get the same focus and care regardless of project size.

**We build for results, not awards.** Our clients need websites that generate calls and enquiries — not designs that look impressive in a portfolio but don't convert. The measure of a good website for a South Wales roofer is whether it brings in work. Everything we build is oriented around that.

**We speak the same language.** Working exclusively with small business owners means we're used to explaining things clearly, without jargon, and being honest when something isn't worth the cost. Our clients aren't digital specialists — they shouldn't need to be.

**We know the local market.** Ranking a tradesperson in Merthyr Tydfil is a different challenge from ranking a professional services firm in London. We understand South Wales, local search dynamics, and what it takes for a small local business to be visible online.

## The Businesses We Work With

Our portfolio reflects this focus. [K Williams Roofing](/portfolio/k-williams-roofing/) — a Merthyr Tydfil roofing contractor who needed to move beyond word of mouth. [IR Energy](/portfolio/ir-energy/) — a renewable energy installer whose SEO campaign generated 50 enquiries in three months. [AK Promotions](/portfolio/ak-promotions/) — an events company whose site generated 2,800 visits and 75 enquiries without any paid advertising. [What's On Merthyr Tydfil](/portfolio/whats-on-merthyr-tydfil/) — a community platform serving local residents.

These aren't marquee clients with unlimited budgets. They're real local businesses that needed proper digital support and got results because of it.

